From 386b7dd488f8b5f2b27d5b2c5af161e2e4f37adc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: campaign <campaign@local>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 04:12:12 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] WIP prefill-decode-arms T0: ONE allocation owner for the
 co-owner KV pair (per-ubatch reserve/publish, consumed by the other arm under
 the shared cursor)

A co-owner pair shares the cells but each cache kept its own search cursor (v_heads), and find_slot() only
searches while apply_ubatch() moves the cursor afterwards.  Two allocating arms could therefore be handed the
same cells in that window, and -- measured -- a warm run scattered a sequence's cells (pos 512 placed in cell 0
while its prompt sat in 512-1023), which moves this fork's tile-FA numerics.

llama_kv_alloc, shared by the pair exactly like v_cells_impl, is now the only place an allocation is decided:
find_slot() searches from the pair's ONE cursor, marks the cells it chose as reserved (invisible to any search,
either arm) and advances that cursor; the real apply_ubatch() commits (prepare()'s dry run does not consume, so
the reservation survives until the ubatch is really applied); a failed prepare or an abandoned batch context
releases its marks.  Every other place that moves a cursor (seq_rm/seq_keep's pull-back to a freed hole, seq_cp's
stream copy, seq_add, a whole-cache restore, clear) moves the pair's one cursor too.

The handshake: the mutex is held across the search/bookkeeping only (microseconds at a ubatch boundary), never
across a compute -- the campaign measured a 2.85 s starvation from a lock held across a decode step.
llama_memory_alloc_sync() is the request-boundary check either arm may call: it reports reservations nothing
applied (a leaked prepare) instead of letting them shrink the cache silently.

LLAMA_KV_ALLOC_SHARED=0 is the A/B kill switch (the legacy two-cursor path).  With it, warm reps scatter and the
text moves (e05c6e16a136); with the shared owner the two-arm run is bit-identical to the single-context
reference in every rep, on both the full-residency shape and the product shape (arena 5000): 480/480 sampled
logits rows, KV cell census identical over all 729 lines, handshake clean at every boundary.
